IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nl-ies`
IMPORT `nl-ies-deadlines`

-- Newfoundland and Labrador Income and Employment Support Act and Regulations -- the applicant's or recipient's
-- questions about income support. Every question calls the rules in nl-ies.l4 and nl-ies-deadlines.l4; nothing is
-- restated. Plain inputs, one per fact the person can state. Amounts are monthly, in Canadian dollars.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Can I get income support`

@export Do I meet the basic conditions for income support under the Income and Employment Support Act (living in the province, having pursued other resources, not applying because of a strike or lockout)?
GIVEN `I am in the province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are physically present in Newfoundland and Labrador
      `days I have been away` IS A NUMBER @desc If you are away from the province, how many days the absence has lasted or will last; 0 if you are here
      `an officer approved my absence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are away, whether an officer of the department approved the purpose of the absence
      `I am away for medical reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are away, whether the absence is for medical reasons
      `I have pursued all my other financial resources` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (and your spouse or cohabiting partner) have pursued every other source of money available to you, such as EI, CPP or support (support under s 38 of the Family Law Act is not required)
      `I am applying because of job action at work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are applying because of a strike or lockout at your workplace
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I meet the basic conditions` IF
    `meets the conditions of eligibility`
        (`lives in the province` `I am in the province` `days I have been away` `an officer approved my absence` `I am away for medical reasons`)
        `I have pursued all my other financial resources`
        `I am applying because of job action at work`

@export Are my liquid assets within the limit for income support under reg s 26 of the Income and Employment Support Regulations?
GIVEN `people in my application` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people your application is for: you, your spouse or cohabiting partner if any, and your dependent children under 18
      `my cash, bank balances and investments, not counting RRSPs` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of cash, bank balances and readily marketable securities and investments of everyone in the application, not counting RRSPs, RESPs, a support trust, prepaid funeral funds or exempt income, in Canadian dollars
      `the value of my RRSPs` IS A NUMBER @desc The total value of Registered Retirement Savings Plans owned by people in the application, in Canadian dollars; 0 if none
      `my RRSPs can be cashed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the RRSPs can be cashed in (liquefied)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my liquid assets within the limit` IF
    `liquid assets are within the limit` `people in my application`
        (`the liquid assets counted` `my cash, bank balances and investments, not counting RRSPs` `the value of my RRSPs` `my RRSPs can be cashed`)

@export Do I pass the income test for an application for income support under reg s 9(3) (my income in the 30 days before applying against the basic and shelter amounts plus 40%)?
GIVEN `adults in my application` IS A NUMBER @desc How many adults (18 or older, or married or cohabiting) are in your application
      `my shelter` IS A `Shelter` @desc Whether you are renting, paying a mortgage on your home, boarding, or have no shelter cost
      `my monthly rent or mortgage payment` IS A NUMBER @desc Your monthly rent, or the principal and interest on the mortgage of your home, in Canadian dollars; 0 if none
      `my net income in the last 30 days` IS A NUMBER @desc The total net income of the people in your application in the 30 days before the date of application (wages, pensions, EI, support and other income that is not exempt), in Canadian dollars
      `the expenses of earning it an officer has allowed` IS A NUMBER @desc The expenses of earning that income which an officer has authorized as a deduction (reg s 11); 0 if none
      `my child benefit adjustment` IS A NUMBER @desc Any child benefit adjustment the department has approved for you (reg s 19(1)(g)); 0 if none or unknown
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I pass the income test` IF
    `passes the s 9(3) income test`
        (`BR for the s 9(3) test` `adults in my application` `my shelter` `my monthly rent or mortgage payment`)
        `my child benefit adjustment` `my net income in the last 30 days` `the expenses of earning it an officer has allowed`

§ `How much income support can I get`

@export What is the most monthly income support I can get under regs ss 13, 16, 18 and 19(1) of the Income and Employment Support Regulations?
GIVEN `adults in my application` IS A NUMBER @desc How many adults (18 or older, or married or cohabiting) are in your application
      `dependent children` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependent children under 18 are in your application
      `I have a spouse or cohabiting partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a spouse or cohabiting partner in the application
      `my home` IS A `Dwelling` @desc Whether you live in an apartment or house, or in a bed sitting room
      `utilities included in my rent` IS A `Utilities included` @desc Which utilities are included in your rent: heat and electricity, heat only, electricity only, or neither
      `my shelter` IS A `Shelter` @desc Whether you are renting, paying a mortgage on your home, boarding, or have no shelter cost
      `my monthly rent or mortgage payment` IS A NUMBER @desc Your monthly rent, or the principal and interest on the mortgage of your home, in Canadian dollars; 0 if none
      `where I live` IS A `Region` @desc Whether you live on the island, in Labrador, or in a coastal Labrador community
      `I pay for heat separately from rent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you maintain a residence where the cost of heat is not included in the rent
      `adults aged 65 or older` IS A NUMBER @desc How many adults in the application are 65 or older (and will still be eligible two months after applying or turning 65)
      `people certified legally blind` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people in the application are certified legally blind by the CNIB or an approved professional
      `people certified with diabetes` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people in the application have diabetes certified by an approved professional
      `someone needs supportive services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an approved professional has certified that someone in the application needs supportive services for daily living
      `my earnings this month` IS A NUMBER @desc Wages, salary, self-employment income and lottery winnings received this month by the people in the application, in Canadian dollars
      `the expenses of earning it an officer has allowed` IS A NUMBER @desc The expenses of earning that income which an officer has authorized as a deduction (reg s 11); 0 if none
      `my other non-exempt income this month` IS A NUMBER @desc Other income this month that counts in full, such as CPP, OAS, EI, workers' compensation, pensions or spousal support, in Canadian dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most monthly income support I can get` MEANS
    `the most monthly income support` (`s 13` PLUS `s 16`) `deducted` `s 19`
    WHERE
        `people` MEANS `adults in my application` PLUS `dependent children`
        `s 13` MEANS `the s 13 amount` `adults in my application` `my home` `utilities included in my rent`
        `s 16` MEANS `the s 16 amount` `my shelter` `adults in my application` `my monthly rent or mortgage payment` `my home` `utilities included in my rent`
        `deducted` MEANS `the income deducted` (`the exemption class` `people` `someone needs supportive services`) `my earnings this month` `the expenses of earning it an officer has allowed` `my other non-exempt income this month`
        `s 19` MEANS `the s 19(1) amounts` `where I live` `I pay for heat separately from rent` `adults aged 65 or older` `people certified legally blind` `people certified with diabetes` (`dependent children` GREATER THAN 0 AND (NOT `I have a spouse or cohabiting partner`))

@export How much of my monthly earnings is exempt (not deducted from income support) under reg s 12(a)?
GIVEN `people in my application` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people your application is for, including dependent children
      `someone needs supportive services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an approved professional has certified that someone in the application needs supportive services for daily living
      `my earnings this month` IS A NUMBER @desc Wages, salary, self-employment income and lottery winnings received this month, in Canadian dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of my earnings is exempt` MEANS
    `the s 12(a) exemption` (`the exemption class` `people in my application` `someone needs supportive services`) `my earnings this month`

§ `What must I report, and by when`

-- Arises once income support is being received.

@export Must I report this change to my officer immediately under s 17(5) of the Act and reg s 7(1)?
GIVEN `what changed` IS A `Change` @desc What has changed: your address, living arrangements, marital or cohabitation status, a dependent's circumstances, income or assets, an absence from the province, the reason you applied, receipt of a liquid asset, a sale or transfer of assets, expenses of earning income, something the minister has said must be reported, or none of these
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I report the change` IF `the change must be reported immediately` `what changed`

@export By what date must I give the information an officer asked for in writing, under reg s 5(2)?
GIVEN `the date of the officer's request` IS A DATE @desc The date on which the officer made the written request
      `extra days the officer allowed` IS A NUMBER @desc Any extra days the officer has allowed beyond the 30 (reg s 5(3)); 0 if none
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I answer the officer` MEANS `the last day to answer` `the date of the officer's request` `extra days the officer allowed`

§ `Reviews and appeals`

-- Arises only when a decision about income support has gone against the person.

@export By what date must I ask in writing for an internal review of a decision about my income support (Act s 41(3))?
GIVEN `the date I was told of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The date on which you were notified of the decision, underpayment or overpayment
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I ask for an internal review` MEANS `the last day to request an internal review` `the date I was told of the decision`

@export By what date must I appeal to the appeal board after an internal review (Act s 43(2))?
GIVEN `the date I received the outcome of the review` IS A DATE @desc The date on which you received the outcome of the internal review (you are considered to have received it 7 business days after it was decided)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I appeal` MEANS `the last day to appeal` `the date I received the outcome of the review`
